From: OnePlus 9 Pro kernel review
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: Don't log an optional PM callback as an error

The rmnet_ctl IPA PM client is registered with a zeroed parameter structure
and intentionally leaves callback unset. ipa_pm_register() stores this NULL
callback, and activate_work_func() still activates the client, completes its
state transition and performs clock scaling. A missing callback in this
activation notification path is therefore expected for this client.

The bugreport contains 105 occurrences of this exact activate_work_func()
warning between 3017.996 and 4442.673 seconds uptime (about 50 to 74 minutes
after boot), so it is not limited to early boot. Remove only this misleading
log in activate_work_func(). Do not change the separate ipa_pm_handle_suspend()
missing-callback WARN_ON path.

This patch changes logging only; it does not change IPA activation, wake locks,
clock votes, packet handling or network behaviour.

---
diff --git a/techpack/dataipa/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa_v3/ipa_pm.c b/techpack/dataipa/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa_v3/ipa_pm.c
--- a/techpack/dataipa/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa_v3/ipa_pm.c
+++ b/techpack/dataipa/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa_v3/ipa_pm.c
@@ -444,8 +444,6 @@
 	if (client->callback) {
 		client->callback(client->callback_params,
 			IPA_PM_CLIENT_ACTIVATED);
-	} else {
-		IPA_PM_ERR_RL("client has no callback");
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&ipa_pm_ctx->client_mutex);
